From: OpenATV RetroGaming <noreply@openatv.local>
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: avoid unbounded playback polling on classic Vu+

The Uno 4K SE vendor PCM can leave the main emulation thread asleep in
poll(..., -1) with the PCM RUNNING, delay zero and all 32768 frames available.
Video then stalls as well; a delayed wakeup only resumes it temporarily.

The PCM is already opened with SND_PCM_NONBLOCK. Try writing before waiting
for POLLOUT and wait at most 20 ms only after EAGAIN. Keep the existing retry
limit and recovery path, and handle zero progress without spinning. This
patch is selected only for the classic Vu+ machine feature. Microphone,
other platforms, audio synchronisation and volume remain unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [classic Vu+ vendor PCM workaround]
--- a/audio/drivers/alsa.c
+++ b/audio/drivers/alsa.c
@@ -328,6 +328,7 @@ static void *alsa_init(const char *device, unsigned rate, unsigned latency,
    if (alsa_init_pcm(&alsa->pcm, device, SND_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK, rate,
             latency, 2, &alsa->stream_info, new_rate, SND_PCM_NONBLOCK) < 0)
       goto error;
+   RARCH_LOG("[ALSA] Vu+ write-first playback with bounded 20 ms waits.\n");
 
    return alsa;
 
@@ -391,7 +392,7 @@ static ssize_t alsa_write(void *data, const void *buf_, size_t len)
 
             break;
          }
-         else if (frames == -EAGAIN)
+         else if (frames == -EAGAIN || frames == 0)
             break;
          else if (frames < 0)
             return -1;
@@ -407,17 +408,22 @@ static ssize_t alsa_write(void *data, const void *buf_, size_t len)
 
       while (size)
       {
-         snd_pcm_sframes_t frames;
-         int rc = snd_pcm_wait(alsa->pcm, -1);
+         /* The descriptor is nonblocking. A missed vendor POLLOUT wakeup
+          * must not stall the emulation thread when it can already write. */
+         snd_pcm_sframes_t frames = snd_pcm_writei(alsa->pcm, buf, size);
 
-         if (rc == -EPIPE || rc == -ESTRPIPE || rc == -EINTR)
+         if (frames == -EAGAIN)
          {
-            if (snd_pcm_recover(alsa->pcm, rc, 1) < 0)
-               return -1;
-            continue;
+            int rc = snd_pcm_wait(alsa->pcm, 20);
+            /* On timeout, retry the nonblocking write: the vendor PCM can
+             * have space without signalling its poll descriptor. Negative
+             * results use the same bounded recovery path as write errors. */
+            frames = rc < 0 ? rc : snd_pcm_writei(alsa->pcm, buf, size);
          }
 
-         frames = snd_pcm_writei(alsa->pcm, buf, size);
+         /* A broken or disappearing PCM must not trap the main loop. */
+         if (frames == 0)
+            break;
 
          if (frames == -EPIPE || frames == -EINTR || frames == -ESTRPIPE)
          {
